## HashMap Internals

```java
static final int hash(Object key) {
    int h;
    return (key == null) ? 0 : (h = key.hashCode()) ^ (h >>> 16);
}
int index = (n - 1) & hash; // fast modulo, n must be power of 2
```

### Treeification
Java 8 converts bucket to Red-Black Tree when bucket length >= TREEIFY_THRESHOLD (8) AND table capacity >= MIN_TREEIFY_CAPACITY (64). Reverts to linked list when <= UNTREEIFY_THRESHOLD (6).

### ConcurrentHashMap vs Hashtable
- Hashtable: single monitor lock on entire map — all threads queue
- ConcurrentHashMap Java 8+: CAS for empty buckets, synchronized on bucket head for collision chains — different buckets write in parallel

## Spring Boot Auto-Configuration

### @SpringBootApplication = 3 annotations
```java
@SpringBootConfiguration   // = @Configuration
@EnableAutoConfiguration   // triggers auto-config
@ComponentScan             // scans current package
```

### Auto-Configuration Mechanism
1. Spring scans META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration.imports
2. Each AutoConfiguration class has @ConditionalOn* guards
3. Only loads if conditions met (class on classpath, bean not already defined)

### Key Conditionals
```java
@ConditionalOnClass(DataSource.class)      // class on classpath
@ConditionalOnMissingBean(DataSource.class) // bean not yet defined
@ConditionalOnProperty("spring.datasource.url") // property present
```

### Bean Lifecycle Hooks
```java
@Component
public class MyBean implements InitializingBean, DisposableBean {
    @PostConstruct void init() { /* after injection */ }
    @PreDestroy void cleanup() { /* before destroy */ }
    public void afterPropertiesSet() { /* InitializingBean */ }
    public void destroy() { /* DisposableBean */ }
}
```

### Startup Order: @PostConstruct → afterPropertiesSet() → @EventListener(ApplicationReadyEvent)

## Spring AOP & Proxies

### Proxy Types
- **JDK Dynamic Proxy**: bean implements interface → proxy wraps the interface
- **CGLIB Proxy**: no interface (or proxyTargetClass=true) → subclass proxy

### @Transactional Self-Invocation Bug
```java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    public void createOrder() {
        saveOrder(); // BUG: direct call bypasses proxy → NO transaction!
    }
    @Transactional
    public void saveOrder() { ... }
}
// Fix 1: inject self via @Autowired OrderService self;
// Fix 2: move saveOrder to separate service
// Fix 3: @EnableAspectJAutoProxy(exposeProxy=true) + (OrderService)AopContext.currentProxy()
```

### Custom Aspect
```java
@Aspect @Component
public class LoggingAspect {
    @Around("@annotation(Loggable)")
    public Object log(ProceedingJoinPoint pjp) throws Throwable {
        log.info("Before: {}", pjp.getSignature());
        Object result = pjp.proceed();
        log.info("After");
        return result;
    }
}
```

### @Transactional Propagation
- REQUIRED (default): join existing or create new
- REQUIRES_NEW: always new transaction (suspend outer)
- SUPPORTS: join if exists, else non-transactional
- NOT_SUPPORTED: always non-transactional

## JWT Authentication in Spring Security

### Custom JWT Filter
```java
@Component
public class JwtFilter extends OncePerRequestFilter {
    @Override
    protected void doFilterInternal(HttpServletRequest req,
            HttpServletResponse res, FilterChain chain) throws Exception {
        String token = extractToken(req);
        if (token != null && jwtUtil.isValid(token)) {
            UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken auth =
                new UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken(
                    jwtUtil.getUsername(token), null,
                    jwtUtil.getAuthorities(token));
            SecurityContextHolder.getContext().setAuthentication(auth);
        }
        chain.doFilter(req, res);
    }
}
```

### SecurityFilterChain Config
```java
@Bean
public SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
    return http
        .csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable())
        .sessionManagement(s -> s.sessionCreationPolicy(STATELESS))
        .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
            .requestMatchers("/api/auth/**").permitAll()
            .anyRequest().authenticated())
        .addFilterBefore(jwtFilter, UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter.class)
        .build();
}
```

### SecurityContextHolder propagation
Default: ThreadLocal — works for synchronous code. For reactive/async: use SecurityContextHolder.setStrategyName(MODE_INHERITABLETHREADLOCAL) or use ReactiveSecurityContextHolder for WebFlux.

## Java Optional

### Core Operations
```java
Optional<User> user = findById(id); // returns Optional.empty() if not found

// Safe access chain
String city = user
    .map(User::getAddress)
    .map(Address::getCity)
    .orElse("Unknown");

// orElse (always evaluates) vs orElseGet (lazy)
User result = user.orElse(new User());             // User() always constructed
User result = user.orElseGet(() -> new User());    // User() only if absent

// Throw if absent
User u = user.orElseThrow(() -> new UserNotFoundException(id));

// Execute if present
user.ifPresent(u -> sendEmail(u.getEmail()));
user.ifPresentOrElse(u -> send(u), () -> log.warn("Not found"));

// Filter
Optional<User> admin = user.filter(u -> u.getRole() == ADMIN);

// flatMap for Optional-returning methods
Optional<String> email = user.flatMap(User::getOptionalEmail);
```

### Anti-Patterns
```java
// WRONG: Optional.get() without isPresent() check
String name = user.get(); // NoSuchElementException if empty!

// WRONG: Optional as field/parameter/collection element
private Optional<String> name; // unnecessary boxing
List<Optional<User>> users;    // just use List<User> with null check

// WRONG: Wrapping and immediately unwrapping
if (Optional.of(value).isPresent()) // just use value != null
```

### Return Optional from methods that may not find a result
```java
public Optional<User> findByEmail(String email) { ... }
// Never return Optional<List<T>> — return empty list instead
public List<User> findByDept(String dept) { return List.of(); } // not Optional<List>

## Modern Java Features

### Records (Java 16+) — Immutable DTOs
```java
// Replaces: class with final fields, constructor, getters, equals, hashCode, toString
public record Point(int x, int y) {}

// Compact constructor (validation)
public record Range(int min, int max) {
    Range { if (min > max) throw new IllegalArgumentException(); }
}

Point p = new Point(1, 2);
p.x(); p.y(); // accessor methods (not getX())
// Records are final — cannot extend
// Records CAN implement interfaces
```

### Sealed Classes (Java 17+) — Closed Type Hierarchy
```java
public sealed interface Shape permits Circle, Rectangle, Triangle {}
public record Circle(double radius) implements Shape {}
public record Rectangle(double w, double h) implements Shape {}

// Exhaustive pattern matching switch (Java 21)
double area = switch (shape) {
    case Circle c    -> Math.PI * c.radius() * c.radius();
    case Rectangle r -> r.w() * r.h();
    case Triangle t  -> ...;
}; // no default needed — compiler knows all cases
```

### Pattern Matching instanceof (Java 16+)
```java
// Old
if (obj instanceof String) { String s = (String) obj; ... }
// New
if (obj instanceof String s) { s.toUpperCase(); } // binding var
```

### Text Blocks (Java 15+)
```java
String json = """
    {
      "name": "Alice",
      "age": 30
    }
    """;
// No escape sequences needed — indentation stripped automatically
```

### Switch Expressions (Java 14+)
```java
int days = switch (month) {
    case JANUARY, MARCH -> 31;
    case FEBRUARY       -> isLeapYear ? 29 : 28;
    default             -> 30;
};
```

## Java Generics Deep Dive

### Bounded Wildcards & PECS
**PECS: Producer Extends, Consumer Super**
```java
// Producer: read from (covariant)
public void process(List<? extends Number> nums) {
    double sum = 0;
    for (Number n : nums) sum += n.doubleValue(); // can READ
    // nums.add(1.0); // COMPILE ERROR — can't write
}

// Consumer: write to (contravariant)
public void addNumbers(List<? super Integer> list) {
    list.add(42); // can WRITE integers
    // Integer n = list.get(0); // COMPILE ERROR — only Object returned
}

// Copy elements: src produces, dest consumes
public <T> void copy(List<? extends T> src, List<? super T> dest) {
    for (T elem : src) dest.add(elem);
}
```

### Why List<String> is not List<Object>
```java
List<String> strings = new ArrayList<>();
// List<Object> objs = strings; // COMPILE ERROR — not covariant
// If allowed: objs.add(42) would corrupt the List<String>!
List<? extends Object> objs = strings; // OK but read-only
```

### Type Erasure
```java
// At compile time: List<String>, List<Integer>
// At runtime: both become raw List — generic info erased
List<String> ls = new ArrayList<>();
List<Integer> li = new ArrayList<>();
System.out.println(ls.getClass() == li.getClass()); // true!
```

### @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
Required when casting erased types. Use @SafeVarargs on varargs methods with generics to suppress heap pollution warning.

## Java Collections Internals

### Performance Comparison
| Operation | ArrayList | LinkedList | ArrayDeque |
|---|---|---|---|
| get(i) | O(1) | O(n) | O(1) head/tail |
| add(end) | O(1) amortized | O(1) | O(1) amortized |
| add(middle) | O(n) | O(1)* | O(n) |
| remove(i) | O(n) | O(1)* | - |
| Memory | Array + 50% buffer | Node per element (+2 pointers) | Circular array |

*O(1) only with iterator — finding the position is O(n)

### ArrayList Resizing
```java
// When capacity exceeded: grows by 50% (newCapacity = oldCapacity * 3/2)
// new Object[oldCapacity + (oldCapacity >> 1)]
// Use new ArrayList<>(expectedSize) to pre-size and avoid resizing
```

### LinkedList: Avoid for Random Access
LinkedList is actually a Deque — use ArrayDeque instead.
LinkedList: each node = 2 pointers (~48 bytes overhead) → GC pressure.

### ArrayDeque: Preferred Stack & Queue
```java
Deque<Integer> stack = new ArrayDeque<>(); // push/pop
Queue<Integer> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();  // offer/poll
// Circular array: amortized O(1) for all operations
// No null elements allowed (unlike LinkedList)
```

### Fail-Fast Iterators
```java
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList("a", "b", "c"));
Iterator<String> it = list.iterator();
while (it.hasNext()) {
    String s = it.next();
    if (s.equals("b")) it.remove(); // OK: use iterator's remove
    // list.remove(s); // ConcurrentModificationException!
}
// CopyOnWriteArrayList: fail-safe (snapshot), no CME, expensive writes
```

## Java Exception Handling

### Exception Hierarchy
```
Throwable
├── Error (JVM-level: OutOfMemoryError, StackOverflowError) — don't catch
└── Exception
    ├── CheckedException (IOException, SQLException) — must catch or declare
    └── RuntimeException (NPE, IllegalState, ClassCast) — unchecked, optional catch
```

### Custom Exception Hierarchy
```java
public class AppException extends RuntimeException { // prefer unchecked
    private final ErrorCode code;
    public AppException(ErrorCode code, String msg) {
        super(msg); this.code = code;
    }
    public AppException(ErrorCode code, String msg, Throwable cause) {
        super(msg, cause); this.code = code; // chain: preserve root cause!
    }
}
public class UserNotFoundException extends AppException {
    public UserNotFoundException(Long id) {
        super(ErrorCode.USER_NOT_FOUND, "User not found: " + id);
    }
}
```

### try-with-resources (Java 7+)
```java
try (Connection conn = ds.getConnection();
     PreparedStatement ps = conn.prepareStatement(sql)) {
    // auto-closed in reverse order even on exception
    // implements AutoCloseable
} catch (SQLException e) {
    throw new DataAccessException("DB error", e); // chain cause!
}
```

### Best Practices
```java
// WRONG: swallow exception
try { doStuff(); } catch (Exception e) {}

// WRONG: log AND rethrow
try { doStuff(); } catch (Exception e) { log.error(e); throw e; } // double log!

// CORRECT: wrap and chain
try { doStuff(); } catch (IOException e) {
    throw new ServiceException("Failed to process", e); // keep cause
}
```

## Spring Boot REST Best Practices

### Controller Structure
```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/v1/orders")
@Validated
public class OrderController {
    @PostMapping
    public ResponseEntity<OrderResponse> create(
            @Valid @RequestBody CreateOrderRequest request,
            @RequestHeader("X-Idempotency-Key") String idempotencyKey) {
        OrderResponse order = orderService.create(request, idempotencyKey);
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(order);
    }
    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public ResponseEntity<OrderResponse> get(@PathVariable Long id) {
        return ResponseEntity.ok(orderService.findById(id));
    }
}
```

### Bean Validation (JSR-380)
```java
public record CreateOrderRequest(
    @NotBlank String productId,
    @Positive @Max(100) int quantity,
    @NotNull @Valid ShippingAddress address
) {}
```

### Global Error Handler (RFC 7807 ProblemDetail)
```java
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    @ExceptionHandler(UserNotFoundException.class)
    public ProblemDetail handleNotFound(UserNotFoundException ex) {
        ProblemDetail pd = ProblemDetail.forStatusAndDetail(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, ex.getMessage());
        pd.setTitle("User Not Found");
        pd.setProperty("timestamp", Instant.now());
        return pd;
    }
    @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)
    public ProblemDetail handleValidation(MethodArgumentNotValidException ex) {
        ProblemDetail pd = ProblemDetail.forStatus(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
        pd.setProperty("errors", ex.getBindingResult().getFieldErrors().stream()
            .map(e -> e.getField() + ": " + e.getDefaultMessage()).toList());
        return pd;
    }
}
```

