## Spring Cache Abstraction

### Core Annotations
```java
@Service
public class UserService {
    @Cacheable(value = "users", key = "#id")
    public User findById(Long id) { return repo.findById(id).orElseThrow(); }

    @CachePut(value = "users", key = "#user.id") // always update cache
    public User update(User user) { return repo.save(user); }

    @CacheEvict(value = "users", key = "#id") // remove from cache
    public void delete(Long id) { repo.deleteById(id); }

    @CacheEvict(value = "users", allEntries = true) // clear entire cache
    public void clearAll() {}

    @Caching(evict = {@CacheEvict("users"), @CacheEvict("userSummaries")})
    public void deleteWithCleanup(Long id) { repo.deleteById(id); }
}
```

### Conditional Caching
```java
@Cacheable(value="users", key="#id",
    condition="#id > 0",   // cache only if id > 0
    unless="#result == null")  // don't cache null results
```

### Redis TTL Configuration
```java
@Bean
public RedisCacheManager cacheManager(RedisConnectionFactory factory) {
    RedisCacheConfiguration config = RedisCacheConfiguration.defaultCacheConfig()
        .entryTtl(Duration.ofMinutes(10))
        .serializeValuesWith(SerializationPair.fromSerializer(new GenericJackson2JsonRedisSerializer()));
    return RedisCacheManager.builder(factory)
        .withCacheConfiguration("users", config.entryTtl(Duration.ofMinutes(5)))
        .withCacheConfiguration("products", config.entryTtl(Duration.ofHours(1)))
        .build();
}
```

### Cache Stampede Prevention
When cache expires, many requests hit DB simultaneously:
- **Locking**: only one thread refreshes, others wait
- **Probabilistic Early Expiration**: randomly refresh before TTL expires
- **Two-level cache**: Caffeine (L1 in-process) + Redis (L2 distributed)

